Host-side project tests (no hardware required, run from the project root):

- node test/decoder.test.js
    Decoder regression tests for chirpstack/decoder.js: CayenneLPP metric and
    imperial (rain/pressure resolution), debug channels (Generic Sensor and
    legacy Analog Input), binary version 1 (older firmware) and unknown
    versions.

- node test/payload_roundtrip.test.js
    Compiles src/payload_binary.cpp together with test/payload_roundtrip.cpp
    for the host (c++/g++/clang++, CXX overrides; skipped if none is found),
    encodes known measurement sets (metric, imperial, minimal, out of range)
    and checks that decoder.js returns the same values - and clamps instead
    of wrapping.

These are plain Node.js scripts, not PlatformIO unit tests; `pio test` is
not used in this project.
